      "writtenOn": "2017-02-28T23:01:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wording is confusing here. This is my suggested rewording (not including @links)\n\n\nThis class contains methods for managing IPsec sessions, which will perform kernel-space\nencryption and decryption of socket or Network traffic.\n\n\u003cp\u003e\nTo establish an IPsec connection for a socket, users first must follow these steps.\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreate an IpSecTransform.\n\u003cli\u003eReady the transform by calling activateTransform.\n\u003cli\u003eApply the transform to a socket with applyTransportModeTransform.\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\nUsers should take care to clean up after completion by calling removeTransportModeTransform and then calling deactivateTransform.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 53,
        "endChar": 88
      },
      "revId": "0113501f58b7405f2dfa8a27d6291a16ec7f1f68",
